{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1103506-apparently-ww-paradox-is-discussing-a-w-ta-game-at-e3-anyone-have-any-details","id":1103506,"title":"Apparently WW/Paradox is discussing a W:tA game at E3--anyone have any details?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-14T08:32:33-07:00","id":1103506,"title":"Apparently WW/Paradox is discussing a W:tA game at E3--anyone have any details?","content":"I just saw a post on Facebook about this with a couple of photos of people at a booth sitting around a TV with the game title (or maybe it's promotional art of the game title). Either way the post went up 14 hours ago, and there are still no details about this game--hell the actual website (<a href=\"http://www.werewolf-videogame.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.werewolf-videogame.com/</a>) is still uncompleted.<br /> <br /> Does anyone know anything they can share about this or the game? I'm chomping at the bit over here with a mixed anticipation and trepidation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T11:43:48-07:00","id":1103561,"title":"","content":"Howdy!<br /> <br /> \u200bI've also been aggressively looking for information on a near daily basis since the game was initially announced. Luckily I found this today.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://rpgamer.com/news/Q2-2017/061417b.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpgamer.com/news/Q2-2017/061417b.html</a><br /> <br /> <br /> Not a lot to go on honestly.<br /> <br /> \u200bSome concept art.<br /> \u200bGifts are in (referred to as magic and spirit stuff in the article).<br /> Wyrm is misspelled :3<br /> Frenzy will have a rage meter that can cause you to gain an increase in lethality but make it difficult to differentiate between friend and foe. Frenzy/Rage can also occur during dialogue.<br /> <br /> \u200bNot much at all to go on as the game is still a looooong ways out, but enough to wet out muzzles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12474-cavebear56","name":"cavebear56","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T13:54:19-07:00","id":1103604,"title":"","content":"Meh. My prediction: This thing will make some noise for a year or so and slowly fizzle like the last two or three W:tA computer games.<br /> <br /> \u200bReason: To do Werewolf right, it can't be too linear -- it's got to give you the option to think. That means a fairly robust playspace or world (Skyrim would be a pretty good analogy on this point). That's expensive for a game that has only a limited target audience. Alternately, it could appeal to the lowest common denominator and go straight to being an FPS (first-person-slasher), which has the downside of putting it in direct competition with the rest of all the cheap/quick/stupid crap out there on the market already. The example that comes to mind would be the Shadowrun videogame -- whose entire concept apparently was to build an extraordinarily crappy FPS and grab a few extra sales by slapping the Shadowrun name on the box to tap into the &quot;cult following&quot;.<br /> <br /> As much as I think Werewolf would make a great video game, even I have to admit that that doesn't include &quot;great&quot; in the financial sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T14:06:47-07:00","id":1103608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1103506-apparently-ww-paradox-is-discussing-a-w-ta-game-at-e3-anyone-have-any-details?p=1103604#post1103604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bReason: To do Werewolf right, it can't be too linear -- it's got to give you the option to think.</div> </div> </div> </div>You sure you're not thinking of Mage? Because otherwise, that doesn't sound like a completely accurate representation of Werewolf. <br /> <br /> Sure, appealing to the open-ended decision making in an RPG is great and does capture the feel of the open-endness of a TRPG, but paramount to Werewolf specifically? Not really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T14:12:32-07:00","id":1103610,"title":"","content":"I hope it comes true, we need this game like yesterday, so please be possitive and supportive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T16:56:25-07:00","id":1103652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1103506-apparently-ww-paradox-is-discussing-a-w-ta-game-at-e3-anyone-have-any-details?p=1103604#post1103604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meh. My prediction: This thing will make some noise for a year or so and slowly fizzle like the last two or three W:tA computer games.<br /> <br /> \u200bReason: To do Werewolf right, it can't be too linear -- it's got to give you the option to think. That means a fairly robust playspace or world (Skyrim would be a pretty good analogy on this point). That's expensive for a game that has only a limited target audience. Alternately, it could appeal to the lowest common denominator and go straight to being an FPS (first-person-slasher), which has the downside of putting it in direct competition with the rest of all the cheap/quick/stupid crap out there on the market already. The example that comes to mind would be the Shadowrun videogame -- whose entire concept apparently was to build an extraordinarily crappy FPS and grab a few extra sales by slapping the Shadowrun name on the box to tap into the &quot;cult following&quot;.<br /> <br /> As much as I think Werewolf would make a great video game, even I have to admit that that doesn't include &quot;great&quot; in the financial sense.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Or they could make it like bloodlines or a bioware type rpg. I Mean Bloodlines isn't full skyrim go anywhere vampire but its a pretty good adaptation. You can't adapt 1 for 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T18:50:56-07:00","id":1103683,"title":"","content":"I think a WtA game can't just do what either VtM video games or the Hunter video games did. There's two big points there. First, all of those games (even the less cult-hit Redemption) are built on video game styles that we know work. Redemption is a pretty basic 3D cRPG, Bloodlines is a FPS/cRPG hybrid that was well established before hand, and the Hunter games were all Gauntlet style games. So all they needed to do was to layer WoD on top of well trod game play styles.<br /> <br /> The biggest hurdles for WtA are the pack, and the structure. The pack is an issue because video games really don't do, &quot;group of characters one player controls&quot; well without either (1) a single character still being the main character and the rest being regulated to support ones or (2) the group gets bland because there's minimal chance to develop each character equally. Generally video games seem to like the &quot;main character with support NPCs&quot; approach, because it lets the development of those NPCs come with player buy in (talk to NPC teammate a lot, slowly unlock missions that help flush out the character's story). But this locks those NPCs into being specific characters. You don't get to build &quot;your pack&quot; but drive the pack the video game hands you; which also tends to favor specific player character choices.<br /> <br /> The structure of the game is also a tough choice. Something like Bloodlines is hard on making the pack important. Something like Redemption makes it hard to really touch on a lot of the basic stuff Werewolf does.<br /> <br /> Were I involved in any of this, I would point towards what Harebrained Scheme's did with Shadowrun Returns. They don't do anything that solves the pack issue, but having more relatively short scenarios that you can play through and that explore different aspects of the setting seems a pretty compelling model for a WtA game over the single plotline approach. A decent selection of 10-20 hour plots that let you explore different things without trying to shove it all in one story could be good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T19:24:46-07:00","id":1103692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1103506-apparently-ww-paradox-is-discussing-a-w-ta-game-at-e3-anyone-have-any-details?p=1103604#post1103604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meh. My prediction: This thing will make some noise for a year or so and slowly fizzle like the last two or three W:tA computer games.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd take that bet.<br /> <br /> The two previously unreleased Werewolf games did not have the same circumstances surrounding it that this one does. Cyanide and FHI can do this game successfully in a number of ways, and I'm fairly positive they will.<br /> <br /> Will the game be amazing, AAA and groundbreaking? No. Not likely. Will this game appeal to hardcore WtA fans, and fans of werewolves and horror in general? Yes. Yes, I think so. <br /> <br /> We'll see over the next three years...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T20:55:40-07:00","id":1103706,"title":"","content":"Basically, I'm just hoping for Vampire: The Masquerade: Bloodlines except for Werewolf.<br /> <br /> Who isn't?<br /> <br /> I just want your character wandering around New York, the New York Caern, and trying to figure out whether you'll join the Bonegnawer/Glass Walker pack, the Shadow Lords, or the Silver Fangs.<br /> <br /> Will it be bad to be solo?<br /> <br /> A little but Bloodlines was awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T23:45:36-07:00","id":1103735,"title":"","content":"I'm most certainly not.<br /> <br /> I think being forced to play being a solo werewolf for the whole game would feel decidedly not WtA. The whole &quot;pick your faction&quot; that's essential to vampire politics is silly in Garou politics where the games heavily encourage PCs to be unification oriented characters in the divided Nation.<br /> <br /> So no pack, vampire politics instead of werewolf ones, and then the whole Umbra aspect of things to address? Yeah. I don't think VtMB with a furry reskin would be a good path to take. VtMB is a fun game, but it works because it's a decent FPS/cRPG hybrid that feels VtM, which can't just have werewolves swapped for vampires and work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T23:50:23-07:00","id":1103738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1103506-apparently-ww-paradox-is-discussing-a-w-ta-game-at-e3-anyone-have-any-details?p=1103735#post1103735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm most certainly not.<br /> <br /> I think being forced to play being a solo werewolf for the whole game would feel decidedly not WtA. The whole &quot;pick your faction&quot; that's essential to vampire politics is silly in Garou politics where the games heavily encourage PCs to be unification oriented characters in the divided Nation.<br /> <br /> So no pack, vampire politics instead of werewolf ones, and then the whole Umbra aspect of things to address? Yeah. I don't think VtMB with a furry reskin would be a good path to take. VtMB is a fun game, but it works because it's a decent FPS/cRPG hybrid that feels VtM, which can't just have werewolves swapped for vampires and work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. that's not the way I play werewolf.<br /> <br /> I play very heavily political Werewolf games about rank, standing, infighting, reknown, and power games. The Garou Nation is basically Game of Thrones with fur as well as claws. Mind you, Bioware does a good job with &quot;Pack&quot; Companions but I think that it's better to go solo as you don't want a party of fighters in a game like this.<br /> <br /> I think the game should end with you forming a pack rather than playing with one. Maybe getting your fellow garou to join together for the final battle at the end but not before. I also hope there's an option to join Pentex.<br /> <br /> What I really want from the game, though is a chance to explore Garou politics and society as well as history plus lots and lots of smaller adventures. The thing V:TM:B did best was that it really told you, &quot;This is what vampire life is like.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'd like the same for werewolf.<br /> <br /> * You make your change<br /> * You discover Garou society<br /> * You make friends<br /> * You decide what you believe in the setting<br /> * You explore the WOD<br /> * You get to know Pentex<br /> * You explore a Caern's members<br /> * Help in the local power struggles<br /> * Kill some Banes<br /> * Explore the Umbra<br /> <br /> And so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-15-2017, 02:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T03:26:15-07:00","id":1103759,"title":"","content":"I still would love to see a W:tA skin/recode for (or done in the same way of) XCOM, because the missions, story, home base/Caern, gear-up, advancement, and pack tactics would work so well IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T05:54:39-07:00","id":1103780,"title":"","content":"Garou are primarily close combat fighters, so a reskin of X-Com would be silly. It would also violate the theme of WtA to industrially produce Fetishes and Talens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T07:40:54-07:00","id":1103805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1103506-apparently-ww-paradox-is-discussing-a-w-ta-game-at-e3-anyone-have-any-details?p=1103780#post1103780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Garou are primarily close combat fighters, so a reskin of X-Com would be silly. It would also violate the theme of WtA to industrially produce Fetishes and Talens.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why you wouldn't industrially produce fetishes and talens, and you would take advantage of their superior movement speed and durability. It's like you get to be the chryssalid, minus the making new chryssalids thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T09:39:51-07:00","id":1103834,"title":"","content":"Why would it be a non-squad game? Bioware isn't the only company that can do good squad character writing, after all. Besides, one of the key themes of werewolf is that the pack is the most important unit, even if the NPC writing can at times be a bit contrary to that.<br /> <br /> Bloodlines worked as a solo game, because ignorance was assumed and in vampire society, every vampire is on their own in the end. With Werewolf, the pack is the core of your life, and taking it away would gut the setting. I mean, in bloodlines, the PC doesn't actually ever attend meetings or get to know fellow neonates. That takes away sept life as well, which would easily be your quest hub in the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 06-15-2017, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T09:49:14-07:00","id":1103836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1103506-apparently-ww-paradox-is-discussing-a-w-ta-game-at-e3-anyone-have-any-details?p=1103780#post1103780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Garou are primarily close combat fighters, so a reskin of X-Com would be silly. It would also violate the theme of WtA to industrially produce Fetishes and Talens.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI think they meant the style. I.e. turn based RPG. It very well could work with the concept of the Umbra being like the Matrix in the Shadowrun Returns series. Fetishes and talens could easily be handled as rare/extremely rare gear that is gathered via certain quest chains or a craft system (but make the &quot;materials&quot; difficult to forge). <br /> <br /> \u200bObviously when you make a game of an existing property concessions are to be made for the sake of the video game experience of it. Hence why Total War: Warhammer isn't 100% lore/TT accurate as liberties are taken for game balance and game enjoyment.<br /> <br /> \u200bIf I recall I read somewhere they were looking at a third person type of action game, I'll try to dig the old article up somewhere. I'd love for a pack experience and feel it is central but a solo character experience would also be just as enjoyable. Pack experience could work similar to say something like Xenoblade Chronicles X, either pre-determined characters that you have control over/switch on the fly (and it was also real time third person rpg). Likewise they could go the route of Temple of Elemental Evil or Wasteland 2 where we make a pack.<br /> <br /> \u200bA solo character experience though, similar to Bloodlines, would work just fine as long as their are NPC packmates you interact with during the game. It is no different than the vast majority of games released where you have AI partners. From Gears of War, Last of Us or Binary Domain. In fact Binary Domain had group dynamics, dialogue and interactions that affected how your character functioned with them (which applied in game and not just some random cutscene stuff like Bioware pukes out).<br /> <br /> \u200bIts a flexible IP and I'm curious to see how they approach it. I've had the dream, also very slowly programming for years, a Metroidvania style Vampire game. Locations being different settings like a Sabbat City, Tzimisce castle, Nosferatu sewer system. Ultimately, I hope the Werewolf game is a start to them expanding the IP into different game styles that can appeal to different itches.<br /> <br /> \u200bObviously enough I wouldn't want to see a World of Darkness Kart Racing game...hmmm.Or maybe I would... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12474-cavebear56","name":"cavebear56","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T18:19:03-07:00","id":1104072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cavebear56</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1103506-apparently-ww-paradox-is-discussing-a-w-ta-game-at-e3-anyone-have-any-details?p=1103836#post1103836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bIts a flexible IP and I'm curious to see how they approach it. I've had the dream, also very slowly programming for years, a Metroidvania style Vampire game. Locations being different settings like a Sabbat City, Tzimisce castle, Nosferatu sewer system. Ultimately, I hope the Werewolf game is a start to them expanding the IP into different game styles that can appeal to different itches.<br /> <br /> \u200bObviously enough I wouldn't want to see a World of Darkness Kart Racing game...hmmm.Or maybe I would... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... X-Com style is usually the go-to suggestion, but a Metroidvania done in the vein of Portrait of Ruin where you move pack members around could work too...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T23:06:47-07:00","id":1104170,"title":"","content":"Bloodlines was a very focused view of the Vampire setting with some liberties taken. There is alot they didn't do. Alot of options not available. But its generally thought to both be a good game and good Vampire game.<br /> <br /> Werewolf should focus the same on a paring down of the setting. You make a character who goes through their first change. YOu pick auspice, you have a subset of the tribes available as options then you get to pick up your pack as you are introduced to various npcs along the way. Probably don't engage with Fera except as potential npcs out side your pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T23:30:33-07:00","id":1104174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1103506-apparently-ww-paradox-is-discussing-a-w-ta-game-at-e3-anyone-have-any-details?p=1104170#post1104170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bloodlines was a very focused view of the Vampire setting with some liberties taken. There is alot they didn't do. Alot of options not available. But its generally thought to both be a good game and good Vampire game.<br /> <br /> Werewolf should focus the same on a paring down of the setting. You make a character who goes through their first change. YOu pick auspice, you have a subset of the tribes available as options then you get to pick up your pack as you are introduced to various npcs along the way. Probably don't engage with Fera except as potential npcs out side your pack.</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing I really liked about Bloodlines was that it took its time explaining the setting through Santa Monica ---&gt; Hollywood. Once that was done, they threw you up for a loop in Chinatown, where the typical setting rules were changed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T01:21:51-07:00","id":1104196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1103506-apparently-ww-paradox-is-discussing-a-w-ta-game-at-e3-anyone-have-any-details?p=1104170#post1104170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bloodlines was a very focused view of the Vampire setting with some liberties taken. There is alot they didn't do. Alot of options not available. But its generally thought to both be a good game and good Vampire game.<br /> <br /> Werewolf should focus the same on a paring down of the setting. You make a character who goes through their first change. YOu pick auspice, you have a subset of the tribes available as options then you get to pick up your pack as you are introduced to various npcs along the way. Probably don't engage with Fera except as potential npcs out side your pack.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty much how I'd do the game.<br /> <br /> One thing I really liked about Bloodlines which was a failure in the previous game was that there was a big focus on the fact you interacted with mortals. Yes, you primarily dealt with vampires and ghouls but you also had to deal with the regular people of Los Angeles too. You really felt like you were in a World of Darkness and that made a better setting, I think. One of the early missions had you dealing with a human serial killer and that felt interesting and innovative because it was a human monster who had bitten off much more than he could chew with a literal one.<br /> <br /> I hope they use the Werewolf signature characters in this game, which would probably set it in New York.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T05:33:39-07:00","id":1104240,"title":"","content":"+1 for the character creation proccess.(aka breed, auspice and tribe).<br /> Would have been nice to have a differend beginning depending on the breed you choose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T10:38:03-07:00","id":1104357,"title":"","content":"As someone who loves Bloodlines(and is likely my favorite game of all time) and would love to see elements from Bloodlines brought over to the Werewolf game, I simply don't see it happening.<br /> <br /> Bloodlines was/is one of a kind. I don't think we'll ever get anything like Bloodlines ever again. The mood, the sexiness, the characters, the story, the...GRIME. It just FELT like you were in A World of Darkness. And that's something that I just can't see happening again. Not today. <br /> <br /> And that sucks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T10:52:23-07:00","id":1104367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1103506-apparently-ww-paradox-is-discussing-a-w-ta-game-at-e3-anyone-have-any-details?p=1104357#post1104357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> the sexiness</div> </div> </div> </div>please, not in a werewolf game <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T11:06:16-07:00","id":1104375,"title":"","content":"I agree that Bloodlines would not work for WtA because Garou are radically different from Kindred. Rage and Gnosis are not equivalent to Blood Pool and Gifts are not really equivalent to Disciplines. The strength of the Garou are their ability to take alternate forms, there ability to travel into the Umbra, and the fact that they protect the Veil with the Delirium (the fact that the vast majority of human beings run from and cannot accurately remember the event that triggered the Delirium is a wonderful thing for the Garou).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T11:22:34-07:00","id":1104384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1103506-apparently-ww-paradox-is-discussing-a-w-ta-game-at-e3-anyone-have-any-details?p=1104375#post1104375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Delirium is a wonderful thing for the Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>It still can create panic and attract local authorities and wyrm agents <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> And that would have been a nice element for the pc version, or even a part of the Rage - Gnosis dilemma.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T11:25:43-07:00","id":1104387,"title":"","content":"They could have a Veil meter that fluctuated according to how much you turn into Crinos in public. As it got lower, more powerful hunters would start to appear until you started facing Navy SEALS equipped with silver weapons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T11:59:39-07:00","id":1104402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1103506-apparently-ww-paradox-is-discussing-a-w-ta-game-at-e3-anyone-have-any-details?p=1104367#post1104367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> please, not in a werewolf game <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ain't nothing wrong with Mari Cabrah, friend.<br /> <br /> :<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1103506-apparently-ww-paradox-is-discussing-a-w-ta-game-at-e3-anyone-have-any-details?p=1104375#post1104375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree that Bloodlines would not work for WtA because Garou are radically different from Kindred. Rage and Gnosis are not equivalent to Blood Pool and Gifts are not really equivalent to Disciplines. The strength of the Garou are their ability to take alternate forms, there ability to travel into the Umbra, and the fact that they protect the Veil with the Delirium (the fact that the vast majority of human beings run from and cannot accurately remember the event that triggered the Delirium is a wonderful thing for the Garou).</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I figure that if you do that a few times in public, you should be killed by the Elders for breaking the veil. In the modern age, you can justify that by the ubiquitousness of cameras.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> In fact, it'll be fun really to play with the sexiness of the werewolves because for most of the Garou, it'll be &quot;look but don't touch.&quot; Just like with the fact the vampires can't have sex, only feed, Garou can't have sex with other Garou and that'll be a decent justification to keep players from wanting the game to be a romance simulator or Overwatch.<br /> <br /> As for whether or not V:TM: Bloodline is something which can be recreated, I think that's largely a matter of fidelity to the source material.. The developers of W:TA are the same people developing the Call of Cthulhu game so they clearly know how to make atmosphere and mood (albeit the graphics look Xbox 360 than Xbox One--it's cool, I can deal with that) with really a focus on roleplaying over roll-playing.<br /> <br /> I don't want to kill hundreds of Banes in a werewolf game. I want to learn about the Litany and talk about Garou lore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-16-2017, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T13:30:36-07:00","id":1104457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1103506-apparently-ww-paradox-is-discussing-a-w-ta-game-at-e3-anyone-have-any-details?p=1104387#post1104387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They could have a Veil meter that fluctuated according to how much you turn into Crinos in public. As it got lower, more powerful hunters would start to appear until you started facing Navy SEALS equipped with silver weapons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah Navy SEALS that fall into delirium and raise your meter higher hahaha <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> But yup thats the whole concept <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1290