y/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-18T21:51:05-07:00","id":1105284,"title":"","content":"There's a rather long thread on these forums (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1103806-vampire-the-masquerade-fifth-edition-pre-alpha-playtest\">here</a>) that is all about the same. It's a long read (up to 20 pages today), but you kind of get the gist of it in the first few pages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T06:36:45-07:00","id":1105364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1103506-apparently-ww-paradox-is-discussing-a-w-ta-game-at-e3-anyone-have-any-details?p=1104487#post1104487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bThat plot element alone would derail, like, <i>half </i>of W:tA... Albrecht would immediately have to abdicate (with nobody even halfway qualified to take over), probably would have to divest the Silver Crown (Solemn Lord too, probably)... and would also have to be explained how he continued to wear the Silver Crown for however many years since this little tryst went off without the Crown simply disappearing into the Deep Umbra to wait for the next Worthy-Hero to retrieve it... Etc. etc. etc.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut a Silver Fang Metis Cub who's deranged and merely <i>thinks</i> he's Albrecht and Mari's kid... Heh...</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean a Black Fury Metis Cub.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T09:52:05-07:00","id":1105431,"title":"","content":"I liked the horror concept art of the fomori-horror stuff they made, looks quite promising.<br /> <br /> I also liked the two crinos art, they look like skiny metis, but I get quite intrigued by the outworldly way they look. (<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><i>like look like look <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></i>)<br /> <br /> The wasted industrial territory picture could have easily been in a werewolf book, it reminds me an improved artwork from an old 3rd edition book and made me sigh in romantic melancholy, remembering my first innocent sessions I ran back in time.<br /> <br /> The moot gathering is beautiful, could have been better, but still an anouncement that there will be included such elements in the game.<br /> I like the idea of the pack but I worry about the system of the game play, I would like the game to have a pack attack system that will work depending on the skill level of the packmates, so a city boy glass walker might be a problem if you poot him in the front line against a huge wyrm lizard (no that wasnt a sexual innuendo <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />). But if he had a gift that could distract the monster he might be a good asset to play as a backup<br /> <br /> One thing I didn't like, was the possibility that you will not make your own character but there will be ready made characters that will be modified later on in the game.<br /> Please Cyanide don't take that from us !!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","user":"Story Letter","date":". 06-19-2017, 01:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T10:11:50-07:00","id":1105439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1103506-apparently-ww-paradox-is-discussing-a-w-ta-game-at-e3-anyone-have-any-details?p=1105186#post1105186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, watch out for signature characters who are serial killer Lupus transwomen, pedophile Metis intersex, and cannibal Homid transmalen if it is anything like V5. The Thrall of the Wyrm will also probably become the default frenzy, so now can keep things 'edgy'.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is vampire, though. What we have seen from them about werewolf is more focused on garou wanting to kill humans en masse and not caring about your social justice, even if they are freaking Black Furies.<br /> <br /> And given the MET book, Red Talons are now the torture obsessed cultists with huge numbers, potentially.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T10:38:38-07:00","id":1105447,"title":"","content":"And my point is supported. I see no reason to even bother with W5 if it is just going to be a game about genocide and torture porn. They might as well go the entire way and have the Get of Fenris planning to exterminate the non-Aryans across the world so they can resurrect the Third Reich.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T12:11:58-07:00","id":1105479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1103506-apparently-ww-paradox-is-discussing-a-w-ta-game-at-e3-anyone-have-any-details?p=1105447#post1105447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And my point is supported. I see no reason to even bother with W5 if it is just going to be a game about genocide and torture porn. They might as well go the entire way and have the Get of Fenris planning to exterminate the non-Aryans across the world so they can resurrect the Third Reich.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fenrir are not natsiz, they are extreme nordic spartans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T14:18:14-07:00","id":1105513,"title":"","content":"After examining it, I think the V5 thing was a very carefully crafted being of controversy bait.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T14:19:40-07:00","id":1105514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1103506-apparently-ww-paradox-is-discussing-a-w-ta-game-at-e3-anyone-have-any-details?p=1105479#post1105479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fenrir are not natsiz, they are extreme nordic spartans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Barring any moral objections, which the Garou DO have on occasion, even the most militant and bloodthirsty Fenrir would consider the Nazis a poor role model. Not the least bit because in the WOD, the Nazis were appropriating Fenrir culture rather than the other way around. The Fenrir, for all of their faults, also kill warriors and monsters not the helpless.<br /> <br /> Which is a weird defense, I can tell you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-19-2017, 06:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T16:00:41-07:00","id":1105541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1103506-apparently-ww-paradox-is-discussing-a-w-ta-game-at-e3-anyone-have-any-details?p=1105479#post1105479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fenrir are not natsiz, they are extreme nordic spartans.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're anti-vikings and anti-northfolk. Anyone who worships or reveres Wotan and his Aesir lackies is going to get it when they roll through, no quarter given.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T16:16:32-07:00","id":1105545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1103506-apparently-ww-paradox-is-discussing-a-w-ta-game-at-e3-anyone-have-any-details?p=1105541#post1105541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They're anti-vikings and anti-northfolk. Anyone who worships or reveres Wotan and his Aesir lackies is going to get it when they roll through, no quarter given.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always felt that was rather dumb to be honest. But there's a lot of weird stuff from the early editions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T00:30:35-07:00","id":1105628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1103506-apparently-ww-paradox-is-discussing-a-w-ta-game-at-e3-anyone-have-any-details?p=1105514#post1105514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Barring any moral objections, which the Garou DO have on occasion, even the most militant and bloodthirsty Fenrir would consider the Nazis a poor role model. Not the least bit because in the WOD, the Nazis were appropriating Fenrir culture rather than the other way around. The Fenrir, for all of their faults, also kill warriors and monsters not the helpless.<br /> <br /> Which is a weird defense, I can tell you.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me, the Sword of Heimindall are such a great example of WtA's themes of the sins of the past. Because that camp, in my headcanon, came from the angry young german youths after WW1. Feeling their country betrayed, feeling the war they fought in or their fathers fought in being wasted. And then there is this guy, spewing the truth. And then you change, and you join the tribe full of people who are STRONG, who are exactly what you want to be as well and who fit in your ideology.<br /> <br /> But after WW2, your kids stand there, hearing the crimes of their parents. Hearing how they let the Wyrm take them over. Now it is their turn to fix things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T07:33:32-07:00","id":1105683,"title":"","content":"Apart from the cultural part of the fenrir tribe, their role model is that of a war-fan that puts war honor above um .. honor.<br /> <br /> More than often a fenrir will choose honor through battle than honor through anything else, I think that war-junkie is the right term.<br /> <br /> Of course this is not a cannon- must always be that way thing, but it will take a realy wise or old (or both) fenrir to partake in all other manners of social-political arts, not to mention that this would be a really rare and precious member of the tribe. The same goes for the Red Talons as well, towards their ''hate hate hate you all hate'' part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T07:58:12-07:00","id":1105693,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://10ztalk.com/2017/06/20/e3-2017-cyanidewerewolf-the-apocalypse-seeks-to-bring-world-of-darkness-to-life/\" target=\"_blank\">https://10ztalk.com/2017/06/20/e3-20...kness-to-life/</a><br /> <br /> \u200bQuick Details<br /> <br /> - No release date<br /> <br /> - Still very conceptual stage<br /> \u200b<br /> - Focus on human/garou relationship (how you deal with the humans to solve problems affects other aspects of the game)<br /> <br /> - Spirit World and spirits to be in (they talk about a waterfall spirit)<br /> <br /> - 3 Forms human (best at interacting with humans and their world), wolf (fastest travel and more in tune with the spirit world) and crinos (best battle form)<br /> \u200b<br /> - Semi open world where you pick a zone from many to go to in any order. What happens within one zone can affect other zones while the game has a central hub (from the description of a forest with spirits could be a caern).<br /> <br /> \u200b- Gave an example of solving a quest for the waterfall spirit its way (shutting down the coal mine) allows you to traverse the waterfall ala Zelda Breath of the Wild (or in their words like a salmon).<br /> <br /> \u200b- You can eat humans but it is not good for your soul. I assume they will be implementing a decay/corrupt/evil/bad meter of some sort.<br /> <br /> \u200b- Also talk about the rage/frenzy mechanic again.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200bSo I'm cautiously optimistic. I hope the corruption mechanic, my word not theirs, doesn't turn into &quot;anything harmful to humans means corruption&quot;. Concerned with a system like that most times anyways since they tend to have &quot;you can play different ways but only one really changes anything and is helpful in how you play!&quot;.<br /> <br /> \u200bFigured 5 forms would be out so not bothered. Still too early for me to really be fearful or doom and gloom though. I'll have to wait to see how a pack is handled or interactions with other garou...or even more about how spirits and the umbra fit in.<br /> <br /> \u200bedit:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.gamewatcher.com/interviews/werewolf-the-apocolypse-interview/12854\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.gamewatcher.com/intervie...nterview/12854</a><br /> <br /> \u200bAnother interview I dug up. Haven't had time to read it, will repost with specifics later but here for anyone to read.<br /> <br /> - Focus on combat, exploration and interaction.<br /> <br /> \u200b- skill tree progression system<br /> <br /> \u200b- Other tribes of garou some friendly others hostile<br /> <br /> \u200b- the waterfall spirit will give more rewards than swimming up it like a salmon (will be essentially a quest giver for a section of a zone)<br /> <br /> - Player choice impacts more gameplay and not overall story<br /> <br /> \u200b- The more you fight in Crinos the more your rage builds.<br /> <br /> \u200b- Pentex is the center of all the corruption appears to take the stage as the big bad (doesn't mean no BSD or more wyrm elements).<br /> <br /> \u200b- stealth is the other major way you can play, the other being combat.<br /> <br /> \u200b- can switch form on the fly. Make a charge in lupus to move quickly but shift into crinos at the last second to hit hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12474,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12474-cavebear56","user":"cavebear56","date":". 06-20-2017, 11:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12474-cavebear56","name":"cavebear56","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T08:17:37-07:00","id":1105700,"title":"","content":"The second interview reveals that all frenzies are completely uncontrolled, no allowance for even packmates. Also, I have reservations against putting Pentex into such a central roll, especially when it's supposed to be ensconsed in corporate inscrutability, in addition to being far from the only game in town.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 06-20-2017, 11:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T09:59:10-07:00","id":1105744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1103506-apparently-ww-paradox-is-discussing-a-w-ta-game-at-e3-anyone-have-any-details?p=1105700#post1105700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I have reservations against putting Pentex into such a central roll, especially when it's supposed to be ensconsed in corporate inscrutability, in addition to being far from the only game in town.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Even as a HUGE fan of Pentex as an enemy, I hope they're a bit more clandestine than what it seems.<br /> <br /> Still, the game is super early. And I'm confident there will be a massive amount of enemy types.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T10:22:43-07:00","id":1105754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1103506-apparently-ww-paradox-is-discussing-a-w-ta-game-at-e3-anyone-have-any-details?p=1105700#post1105700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The second interview reveals that all frenzies are completely uncontrolled, no allowance for even packmates. Also, I have reservations against putting Pentex into such a central roll, especially when it's supposed to be ensconsed in corporate inscrutability, in addition to being far from the only game in town.</div> </div> </div> </div>The general theme they are pushing for, it seems, is garou vs humans. New impegrium is something I have heard, eating humans is bad but can happen,etc. Which, okay, it is interesting, but it kinda goes against the whole 'humans are pawns, not the main baddie'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T10:52:11-07:00","id":1105766,"title":"","content":"I see where they are coming from with it.<br /> <br /> Pentex is a much easier and a safer sell as it plays into that &quot;Corporations are Evil&quot; stereotype commonly used across different mediums and just as, if not more, popular than the &quot;Evil government&quot; trope.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt is a bit easier for people unfamiliar to digest than other avenues of the wyrm. It also helps to give the game more focus, as the wyrm is so expansive to try and have the focus on a cosmic concept of entropy gone mad would be much more difficult to pull off.<br /> <br /> \u200bI still definitely have my concerns but will hold my tongue until it starts to show itself probably in a year we'll see actual gameplay and a more focused vision of what/how the game will be. I will just say we need to remember the game will be making some concessions for the sake of the game itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12474-cavebear56","name":"cavebear56","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T11:05:04-07:00","id":1105770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cavebear56</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1103506-apparently-ww-paradox-is-discussing-a-w-ta-game-at-e3-anyone-have-any-details?p=1105766#post1105766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see where they are coming from with it.<br /> <br /> Pentex is a much easier and a safer sell as it plays into that &quot;Corporations are Evil&quot; stereotype commonly used across different mediums and just as, if not more, popular than the &quot;Evil government&quot; trope.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was talking about other WICs. There are many more commercialized threats that feed the Wyrm than just those subsidiaries under that one holding company, and it's entirely possible that some more ethically stringent corporations might have infections trying to climb the ladder. INTRIGUE!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bIt is a bit easier for people unfamiliar to digest than other avenues of the wyrm. It also helps to give the game more focus, as the wyrm is so expansive to try and have the focus on a cosmic concept of entropy gone mad would be much more difficult to pull off. </div> </div> </div>Cyanide is, at this very moment, teasing their Call of Cthulhu game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bI still definitely have my concerns but will hold my tongue until it starts to show itself probably in a year we'll see actual gameplay and a more focused vision of what/how the game will be. I will just say we need to remember the game will be making some concessions for the sake of the game itself. </div> </div> </div>If you're focusing on corporations and having to do things other than hack and slash, it would probably be a good move to add in a varied range of corporate antagonists not all centered around the same holding company.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T11:05:05-07:00","id":1105769,"title":"","content":"I'm cautiously optimistic for the game based on what's been said.<br /> <br /> My one concern is that the developers might not quite understand, based on the interview, the Sept/Tribe distinction. Unless the game is set in a location where Septs are monotribal.<br /> <br /> I won't lie, I'd be happy with a game that was close to a clone of Bloodlines. It's one of my favorite games ever and actually got me into the World of Darkness tabletop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://paizo.com/campaigns/RageAcrossIreland/gameplay\" target=\"_blank\">My W20 Play-by-Post Game</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2760-formosus","name":"Formosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T11:06:54-07:00","id":1105772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cavebear56</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1103506-apparently-ww-paradox-is-discussing-a-w-ta-game-at-e3-anyone-have-any-details?p=1105693#post1105693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://10ztalk.com/2017/06/20/e3-2017-cyanidewerewolf-the-apocalypse-seeks-to-bring-world-of-darkness-to-life/\" target=\"_blank\">https://10ztalk.com/2017/06/20/e3-20...kness-to-life/</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.gamewatcher.com/interviews/werewolf-the-apocolypse-interview/12854\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.gamewatcher.com/intervie...nterview/12854</a><br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> +1 like from me. love you mate.<br /> <br /> I see a great potential here, that skill tree makes me worried though. Wondering if it will a traditional oWoD kind of ''skill tree'' or something like we see in Styx games, also wondering about Gifts, they will be like the traditional rpg Werewolf or they will be like the ''gifts of the waterfall spirit'' unlocked by various quests it will give you?<br /> <br /> Also, haven't heard anything about a renown system yet and how you might learn new powers, or it will all be an experience point system translated as ''Renown'' instead, in order to learn stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","user":"Story Letter","date":". 06-20-2017, 02:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T11:06:59-07:00","id":1105773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Formosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1103506-apparently-ww-paradox-is-discussing-a-w-ta-game-at-e3-anyone-have-any-details?p=1105769#post1105769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm cautiously optimistic for the game based on what's been said.<br /> <br /> My one concern is that the developers might not quite understand, based on the interview, the Sept/Tribe distinction. <b>Unless the game is set in a location where Septs are monotribal.</b><br /> <br /> I won't lie, I'd be happy with a game that was close to a clone of Bloodlines. It's one of my favorite games ever and actually got me into the World of Darkness tabletop.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's primarily only Europe, and possibly not even any more, given the way that things are going. Then again, they did say that they wanted to focus on Europe at ParaWW...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T11:19:41-07:00","id":1105777,"title":"","content":"Cthulhu is not Werewolf and Werewolf is not Cthulhu. Apples are not Oranges.<br /> <br /> Look, Cthulhu is a well established property across a huge variety of mediums. Werewolf is essentially taking its first steps to a larger audience. So just because Cyanide is doing something with a similar concept (yet handled completely different as a human to Cthulhu mythos has very little in common with a Garou to the Wyrm) doesn't mean it would be a smart move or even easier to implement.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'd be surprised if they don't include other corps that are less &quot;big bad evil corp&quot; as that would be a way to further define the WtA setting. Not all corps are Pentext after all but the fact remains the big bad evil corporation as a central villain is a common stereotype that allows people unfamiliar to quickly form a relevant relation.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat way they don't have to spend a long time spouting off about Pentex and people can jump into the game having the rough idea so its easier to connect. It would be a missed opportunity if they didn't have other companies to highlight the difference and to force players into challenges of morality.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Formosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1103506-apparently-ww-paradox-is-discussing-a-w-ta-game-at-e3-anyone-have-any-details?p=1105769#post1105769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm cautiously optimistic for the game based on what's been said.<br /> <br /> My one concern is that the developers might not quite understand, based on the interview, the Sept/Tribe distinction. Unless the game is set in a location where Septs are monotribal.<br /> <br /> I won't lie, I'd be happy with a game that was close to a clone of Bloodlines. It's one of my favorite games ever and actually got me into the World of Darkness tabletop.</div> </div> </div> </div>My largest concern as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12474,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12474-cavebear56","user":"cavebear56","date":". 06-20-2017, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12474-cavebear56","name":"cavebear56","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T11:52:39-07:00","id":1105788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1103506-apparently-ww-paradox-is-discussing-a-w-ta-game-at-e3-anyone-have-any-details?p=1105773#post1105773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's primarily only Europe, and possibly not even any more, given the way that things are going. Then again, they did say that they wanted to focus on Europe at ParaWW...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't want to derail too much, but based on what I have read (W20 is my first iteration of Werewolf), it seems like the Wendigo would tend toward monotribal Septs in the Americas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://paizo.com/campaigns/RageAcrossIreland/gameplay\" target=\"_blank\">My W20 Play-by-Post Game</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2760-formosus","name":"Formosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T12:00:02-07:00","id":1105791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Formosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1103506-apparently-ww-paradox-is-discussing-a-w-ta-game-at-e3-anyone-have-any-details?p=1105788#post1105788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't want to derail too much, but based on what I have read (W20 is my first iteration of Werewolf), it seems like the Wendigo would tend toward monotribal Septs in the Americas.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Uktena too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T14:30:22-07:00","id":1105843,"title":"","content":"A lot of septs that protect weaker Caerns also tend to be one Tribe affairs since they might only have a dozen Garou. With Garou following their Kinfolk into the Americas, each Tribe would have claimed the closest Caern to their Kinfolk. Whether or not the Uktenu or Wendigo (or any of the native Fera) were able to stop them is another question entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T18:44:43-07:00","id":1105900,"title":"","content":"Uktena only manage it because they have some more significant numbers than other tribes. Also, they have a keen interest in keeping secrets within the tribe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Formosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1103506-apparently-ww-paradox-is-discussing-a-w-ta-game-at-e3-anyone-have-any-details?p=1105788#post1105788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't want to derail too much, but based on what I have read (W20 is my first iteration of Werewolf), it seems like the Wendigo would tend toward monotribal Septs in the Americas.</div> </div> </div> </div>They'd like it, but it probably isn't happening nearly as often as they like for a number of different reasons, like how the Wendigo aren't really all that populous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T18:51:37-07:00","id":1105905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cavebear56</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1103506-apparently-ww-paradox-is-discussing-a-w-ta-game-at-e3-anyone-have-any-details?p=1105777#post1105777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cthulhu is not Werewolf and Werewolf is not Cthulhu. Apples are not Oranges.<br /> <br /> Look, Cthulhu is a well established property across a huge variety of mediums. Werewolf is essentially taking its first steps to a larger audience. So just because Cyanide is doing something with a similar concept (yet handled completely different as a human to Cthulhu mythos has very little in common with a Garou to the Wyrm) doesn't mean it would be a smart move or even easier to implement.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'd be surprised if they don't include other corps that are less &quot;big bad evil corp&quot; as that would be a way to further define the WtA setting. Not all corps are Pentext after all but the fact remains the big bad evil corporation as a central villain is a common stereotype that allows people unfamiliar to quickly form a relevant relation.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat way they don't have to spend a long time spouting off about Pentex and people can jump into the game having the rough idea so its easier to connect. It would be a missed opportunity if they didn't have other companies to highlight the difference and to force players into challenges of morality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would other WICs be <i>less</i> big bad evil corporations? Corporations can ramp up the evil pretty damned quickly, with or without some nebulous support from beyond that may or may not still even apply. Also, Werewolf has a kind of history with adding on new threats of this type. Shinzui, though dedicated to the Weaver, is arguably able to gut Pentex and its holdings. You need more corrupt asshole companies in the event that this occurs, so that the threat remains. Adding them to a video game just means that the old and new fans have something to shake them up a bit. It doesn't really dilute anything; in fact, it would just reinforce it and allow the game lore to move in a direction that it should have a long time ago. I mean, other games that feature megacorporations as major antagonist factions don't just have one; settings like Shadowrun and Cyberpunk, which have some major influence on how the WoD shaped up (Tom Dowd, who produced the ST system, worked on the former), having a fluctuating and changing list of cutthroat corporate raiders who are typically involved in all manner of terrible shit, even if they're ostensibly &quot;good&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T20:59:47-07:00","id":1105931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cavebear56</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1103506-apparently-ww-paradox-is-discussing-a-w-ta-game-at-e3-anyone-have-any-details?p=1105777#post1105777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cthulhu is not Werewolf and Werewolf is not Cthulhu. Apples are not Oranges.<br /> <br /> Look, Cthulhu is a well established property across a huge variety of mediums. Werewolf is essentially taking its first steps to a larger audience. So just because Cyanide is doing something with a similar concept (yet handled completely different as a human to Cthulhu mythos has very little in common with a Garou to the Wyrm) doesn't mean it would be a smart move or even easier to implement.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'd be surprised if they don't include other corps that are less &quot;big bad evil corp&quot; as that would be a way to further define the WtA setting. Not all corps are Pentext after all but the fact remains the big bad evil corporation as a central villain is a common stereotype that allows people unfamiliar to quickly form a relevant relation.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat way they don't have to spend a long time spouting off about Pentex and people can jump into the game having the rough idea so its easier to connect. It would be a missed opportunity if they didn't have other companies to highlight the difference and to force players into challenges of morality.<br /> <br /> My largest concern as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Corporations are, easily, the MOST common enemy you will fight in video games after zombies (and very often they're zombies made by corporations). Even Call of Duty, a game series about the military ended up doing a game about fighting against a PMC that can somehow fight all other nations on Earth simultaneously. This is due to the large influence of cyberpunk, Aliens, and Robocop over many video games. I do foresee Pentex being the primary villain for the game for multiple reasons.<br /> <br /> 1. Pentex is the archenemy of the Garou. The &quot;Wyrm&quot; is effectively Satan so there's no chance of going to Malpheas and fighting it there.<br /> <br /> 2. Pentex is an easy enemy to personify as they're greedy evil corporate executives and they're always a good opponent for left-leaning anarchist gamers from 14 to 40.<br /> <br /> 3. Pentex is basically Weyland-Yutani and mercenaries working for corporations are an easy enemy for non-Werewofl fans to grasp.<br /> <br /> I can't imagine ANYONE other than some pundits at Fox News actually caring also what a mid-tier video game company has to say about capitalism. We don't need any &quot;good&quot; corporations or to defend the feelings of companies everywhere. Not unless you think we need NON-Evil Pharmaceutical Firms in Resident Evil.<br /> <br /> Hell, they should have a Glass Walker Ragabash say this in game.<br /> <br /> &quot;Who are Pentex?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;They're basically Weyland Yutani, OCP, and the Umbrella Corporation all rolled into one. Bad guys with supernatural powers and an even more powerful force: billions and billions of dollars.&quot;<br /> <br /> I mean, seriously, does ANYONE think megacorps need defending or good PR?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T21:15:22-07:00","id":1105933,"title":"","content":"Don't forget to add in the ruthless business culture of Amazon into that mix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T05:29:34-07:00","id":1106011,"title":"","content":"I'm not too bothered by Pentex being a foe, it isn't like Bloodlines had very accurate high level foes, either.<br /> <br /> What I am hoping is that we get to see BSDs being their own thing and not pentex lackies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T07:57:40-07:0