 </div> </div> </div>&quot;Oh my god, JC! A bane!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;A BANE!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T18:14:57-07:00","id":1106353,"title":"","content":"Well they mentioned stealth like three times as one of their &quot;pillars&quot; with combat and speech.<br /> <br /> I'm like, &quot;Stealth is not what I normally associate with Werewolf.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T19:29:56-07:00","id":1106381,"title":"","content":"Yes, an alpha strike from the Umbra is more a Garou thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T20:41:37-07:00","id":1106394,"title":"","content":"In an XCOM-style game, I think it would work really well, even if it was re-skinned for Werewolf: the Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> 1) In XCOM you already get different types of soldiers. Just remake them into the Auspices.<br /> 2) In XCOM each character can have a different Nationality. Make these the Auspices.<br /> 3) In XCOM you could add in a &quot;Breed&quot; if you wanted to, but for the sake of reskinning, just leave them Homid, I suppose.<br /> 4) In XCOM you can customize each character so that they look different.<br /> 5) In XCOM you work for an organization that sends you out on missions all over the world. In Werewolf, your Sept leadership would do the same.<br /> 6) In XCOM you choose the team members you want to have go on the mission. In the Werewolf game you would choose the pack mates you wanted.<br /> 7) In XCOM, you are fighting an alien invasion on the city streets, or in the forests, or in their fortresses. For Werewolf, this is pretty much the same... you almost don't have to change anything, only it's the Wyrm, not aliens.<br /> 8) In XCOM, you level up, learning new skills, acquiring new weapons/tech, or augmenting yourself. These could be normal skills, Gifts, or Fetishes.<br /> 9) In XCOM, you can acquire items needed to advance technology. In Werewolf, these could be spirits and other items necessary for Fetishes.<br /> 10) In XCOM, there's a lot of long-distance combat, but there is close-combat too. In Werewolf, there are gifts that let you do damage from a distance, but most of your combat would be close-quarters.<br /> 11) In XCOM you can upgrade your headquarters. In Werewolf you can enhance your Sept.<br /> 12) In XCOM your team dies... a lot. In Werewolf, everyone dies a lot.<br /> <br /> I mean... that's all just off the top of my head. Obviously it isn't so easy to &quot;reskin&quot;, and you'd need a mechanic for going into War Form (human form you can use guns, in Crinos you are faster and can do more damage with hand-to-hand while healing faster?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T21:48:59-07:00","id":1106414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1103506-apparently-ww-paradox-is-discussing-a-w-ta-game-at-e3-anyone-have-any-details?p=1106353#post1106353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well they mentioned stealth like three times as one of their &quot;pillars&quot; with combat and speech.<br /> <br /> I'm like, &quot;Stealth is not what I normally associate with Werewolf.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Ragabash are definitely capable little stealth wombats. Plus, wolves in general are pretty stealthy. Of course, we tend to have a ton of non-stealth at our tables, but we almost always have at least one character who relies on stealth. Great for getting the drop on unsuspecting enemies who are preoccupied with a pack member, too (remember Clever Girl, the Mokole from Jurassic Park? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) I'm glad that they're including it as a general option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12777-wakuwa","name":"Wakuwa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12777_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}